+# 01: Reserve stock and look up a Reservation
+
+**What to build:** Checkout can reserve stock for a cart in one warehouse and look the Reservation up again by id. A Reservation holds, for each requested SKU, as many units as are Available right now, up to the Requested quantity. Reserved units stop being Available to other Reservations and to directly placed Orders. See the spec (`.scratch/stock-reservations/spec.md`) and ADR 0002 for partial holds. The idempotency key is accepted but replay isn't handled yet (ticket 05).
+
+**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] `ReservationStatus` (ACTIVE, CONFIRMED, RELEASED, EXPIRED) and the `Reservation` dataclass (`reservation_id`, `warehouse`, `items`, `status`, `expires_at`, `order_id`) exist with exactly the fields in the spec and are exported from the package root.
+- [x] `ReservationNotFound`, `ReservationExpired`, `InvalidReservationState` and `IdempotencyConflict` exist, subclass `InventoryError`, and carry attributes as described in the spec.
+- [x] `InventoryService(repository, ledger, clock)` still works unchanged. An optional keyword-only `reservation_ttl` defaults to 20 minutes.
+- [x] `reserve(warehouse, items, idempotency_key)` returns an ACTIVE Reservation with a sequential `RES-0001`-style id, `order_id` None, and `expires_at` = clock now + TTL.
+- [x] Each line holds min(requested, Available). A line with nothing Available is left out of `items`, not included as 0.
+- [x] When no line can hold anything, `InsufficientStock` names the first line in request order, with its requested quantity and available = 0, and no Reservation is created.
+- [x] Unknown warehouse, unknown SKU, or a quantity that isn't a positive integer rejects the whole request (`UnknownWarehouse` / `UnknownSku` / `InvalidQuantity`) and holds nothing. An empty request raises `InvalidOrder`.
+- [x] `get_reservation(id)` returns the Reservation, or raises `ReservationNotFound`.
+- [x] `reserved(sku, warehouse)` sums the units held by ACTIVE Reservations. `available` = on-hand − allocated − reserved, floored at 0. `allocated` is unchanged.
+- [x] A second reserve can't take units held by the first, and `place_order` raises `InsufficientStock` for Reserved units. `place_order` stays all-or-nothing.
+- [x] Reserving writes no ledger entries.
+- [x] Tests go through the public service API with the existing fixtures, and the existing suite passes unchanged.
