+# 02: Reservations expire on their own
+
+**What to build:** An active Reservation that nobody confirms or releases expires at its `expires_at`. From that instant it no longer holds stock, and lookups report it as EXPIRED. There is no sweep or background job: expiry follows from the injected clock alone (ADR 0001).
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Reserve stock and look up a Reservation)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] One instant before `expires_at`, the Reservation is still ACTIVE and its units are still Reserved.
+- [x] At exactly `expires_at`, and any time after, `reserved` no longer counts it and `available` recovers. This works with no other service call in between.
+- [x] `get_reservation` reports EXPIRED once `expires_at` is reached.
+- [x] An expired Reservation's units can be reserved by another cart or taken by `place_order`.
+- [x] A custom `reservation_ttl` passed to the constructor is respected.
+- [x] No code path depends on another call having persisted the EXPIRED status first. Writing it back to storage is optional.
