+# 03: Release a Reservation
+
+**What to build:** Checkout can give up a Reservation (e.g. payment failed or the cart was abandoned), and its units become Available again immediately. Releasing is safe to retry.
+
+**Blocked by:** 02 (Reservations expire on their own)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] Releasing an ACTIVE, unexpired Reservation returns it with status RELEASED, and its units are Available again straight away.
+- [x] Releasing a RELEASED Reservation returns it unchanged with no error.
+- [x] Releasing an expired Reservation returns it unchanged, still EXPIRED, with no error.
+- [x] Releasing a CONFIRMED Reservation raises `InvalidReservationState`. If ticket 04 hasn't landed yet, whichever of 03 and 04 lands second adds this test.
+- [x] Releasing an unknown id raises `ReservationNotFound`.
+- [x] Releasing never writes ledger entries.
