+# 04: Confirm a Reservation into an Order
+
+**What to build:** Once payment succeeds, checkout confirms the Reservation and gets a placed Order for exactly the units it held. Confirming is safe to retry, and never fails for lack of stock, because the Reservation was already a promise.
+
+**Blocked by:** 02 (Reservations expire on their own)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] Confirming an ACTIVE, unexpired Reservation creates a PLACED Order with the next `ORD-` id, `placed_at` = clock now, and lines equal to the Reservation's held items (not the requested quantities).
+- [x] The Reservation becomes CONFIRMED with `order_id` set to the new Order's id.
+- [x] The units move from Reserved to Allocated: on-hand is unchanged, `available` is unchanged by the confirm itself, and nothing is counted twice.
+- [x] Confirming doesn't re-check stock. It still succeeds after a write-off has dropped on-hand below what was reserved.
+- [x] Confirming a CONFIRMED Reservation returns the same Order, even after `expires_at`, and creates no second Order.
+- [x] Confirming an expired Reservation raises `ReservationExpired` and changes nothing.
+- [x] Confirming a RELEASED Reservation raises `InvalidReservationState`. Confirming an unknown id raises `ReservationNotFound`.
+- [x] Shipping or cancelling the resulting Order works as for any Order and leaves the Reservation CONFIRMED.
+- [x] If ticket 03 has landed, add the test that releasing a CONFIRMED Reservation raises `InvalidReservationState`.
