+# 05: Idempotent reserve
+
+**What to build:** The cart service can retry a reserve call safely. Repeating a request with the same idempotency key returns the original Reservation instead of holding stock again. Reusing a key for a different request is rejected. Requests are matched on what the cart *requested*, not on what was held (ADR 0002).
+
+**Blocked by:** 02 (Reservations expire on their own)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] Same key, same warehouse and same requested items (key order irrelevant) returns the original Reservation (same id), and no additional stock is Reserved.
+- [x] A replay after a partial hold returns the original Reservation with its original held items, even if more stock has arrived since. It is never topped up.
+- [x] A replay never changes `expires_at`. A replay after expiry returns the Reservation as EXPIRED. A replay after release or confirm returns its current status.
+- [x] Same key with a different warehouse or different requested items raises `IdempotencyConflict`.
+- [x] Keys are global, not per warehouse, and remembered for the lifetime of the repository.
+- [x] Validation runs before the key lookup: a malformed request reusing a known key gets the validation error, not `IdempotencyConflict`.
+- [x] A reserve that fails (validation, or `InsufficientStock` because nothing could be held) doesn't use up its key. Retrying the same key after stock arrives creates a Reservation.
+
+## Comments
+
+The replay-after-confirm test will be added when ticket 04 (confirm a Reservation) lands.
+
+The replay-after-confirm test (`test_replay_after_confirm_returns_the_reservation_as_confirmed`) was added after ticket 04 landed on `stock-reservations`.
