@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# Inventory
+
+Stock and order bookkeeping for the warehouse service: how many units of each SKU a warehouse holds, and how many of them are already spoken for.
+
+## Stock quantities
+
+**On-hand**:
+Physical units of a SKU in a warehouse.
+_Avoid_: Stock level, physical stock
+
+**Allocated**:
+Units of a SKU promised to placed Orders that have not shipped yet.
+_Avoid_: Committed, reserved (that is a different quantity)
+
+**Reserved**:
+Units of a SKU held by active Reservations. Distinct from Allocated.
+_Avoid_: Held, locked
+
+**Available**:
+Units of a SKU that can still be promised: on-hand minus allocated minus reserved, never below zero.
+_Avoid_: Free stock, ATP
+
+## Orders and reservations
+
+**Order**:
+A customer order fulfilled from a single warehouse.
+_Avoid_: Purchase
+
+**Reservation**:
+A time-limited claim on stock for one cart in one warehouse, taken before payment. It may hold fewer units than the cart asked for.
+_Avoid_: Hold, lock, cart allocation
+
+**Requested quantity**:
+What the cart asked a Reservation to hold for a SKU, as opposed to what it actually holds.
+_Avoid_: Ordered quantity
+
+**Confirm**:
+Turn an active Reservation into a placed Order for exactly the units it holds.
+_Avoid_: Commit, convert
+
+**Release**:
+The cart explicitly gives up an active Reservation, freeing its units.
+_Avoid_: Cancel (reserved for Orders), unreserve
+
+**Expire**:
+An active Reservation reaches its expiry time without being confirmed or released, and stops holding stock.
+_Avoid_: Lapse, time out
