new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b259f36
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0001-reservations-expire-lazily.md
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# Reservations expire lazily, with no sweeper
+
+An active Reservation holds stock only while the injected clock reads before its `expires_at`. Once the clock reaches `expires_at`, every query and command treats the Reservation as expired: reserved totals, lookups, confirm, release, and idempotent replay. Nothing has to run first. We chose this over a periodic sweeper because the package has no scheduler or I/O, all time comes from the injected clock, and stock figures must be correct at any instant rather than only after the next sweep.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A stored status of `ACTIVE` is not the truth on its own. Code that reads Reservations must also compare `expires_at` with the clock. Writing `EXPIRED` back to storage is optional and only a cache.
+- Expiry applies only to `ACTIVE` Reservations. `CONFIRMED` and `RELEASED` are final, so confirming an already-confirmed Reservation still returns its Order after `expires_at`.
