--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0002-reservations-hold-partially-orders-do-not.md
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# Reservations hold partially; orders don't
+
+`reserve` holds, for each requested SKU, as many units as are Available, up to the Requested quantity. SKUs with nothing Available are left out, and `InsufficientStock` is raised only when nothing at all can be held. `place_order` stays all-or-nothing. Checkout wants to go ahead with whatever is in stock and tell the customer about the rest, which it does by comparing the Reservation's items with what it requested. Direct back-office Orders keep their existing all-or-nothing contract.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A Reservation's items can differ from the request, so idempotent replay compares the *requested* items, not the held ones, and the repository keeps the original request alongside the key.
+- The two ways of promising stock deliberately behave differently. Don't "harmonise" them without revisiting this decision with the domain owner.
